# an alias the program calls means the program's own definition of its word where that takes the call, the library's
# else (card alias-follows-redefinition)
'square(x):=x*x*10; 3 squared'	90
'square(x):=x*x*10; squared(2)'	40
# a function's own local of an alias's name binds it only there: another function's xs.push keeps the alias (sample usdcraft)
'f() := { push = 3; push }; g() := { xs = [1]; xs.push(2); xs }; [f(), g()]'	[3, [1, 2]]
